cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use ParallaX, please cite it as below, and cite the SPHEREx data and the catalogues listed on its About page."
title: "ParallaX — SPHEREx blink comparator"
abstract: >-
  A public web tool that blinks SPHEREx visit stacks of any patch of sky, one band at a time on one shared brightness
  scale, so that moving and varying objects can be spotted. Built for the NASA Space Apps Challenge 2026,
  "Planet X and SPHEREx".
type: software
authors:
  - name: "The ParallaX team, NASA Space Apps Challenge 2026"
repository-code: "https://github.com/ABHISHEKSHAHI597/Nasa-Space-Apps-2026"
license: GPL-3.0-or-later
keywords:
  - SPHEREx
  - blink comparator
  - proper motion
  - brown dwarfs
  - citizen science
